    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "And we are back with another edition of the Federalist Radio Hour. I'm Matt Kittle, Senior Elections Correspondent at the Federalist, and your experienced Sherpa on today's quest for knowledge. As always, you can email the show at radio at thefederalist.com. Follow us on X at FDRLST. Make sure to subscribe wherever you download your podcast and, of course, to the premium version of our website as well. Our guest today is Representative Chip Roy, Republican from the great state of Texas representing the fighting 21st congressional district on the heels of the annual March 4 life. movement, March coming up on Friday. It's been an exceptional week for life and the life movement in America. Congressman Roy's legislation has much to do with that. Chief among the bills that he has put out there this week is the Face Act. repeal act of 2025. And just as we begin our conversation, some wonderful news to report on the life movement as well. Congressman Roy, thank you so much for joining us. I appreciate your time and, of course, your mission. You have been one of the great fighters in Congress for some time now on Right to Life issues. This is a big week for that movement, but let's begin with the breaking news today. We have a pardon for political prisoners, do we not in the life movement?",
