  {
    "episode_id": 46642,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46642.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Well, I hope so. I've been reasonably patient with my colleagues. At an election year, we had a lot of stuff going on last year. We've been given the trifecta. We've got a lead. The president is leading. There's no excuse now. The president has set the standard that these political prosecutions, political prosecutions, shouldn't stand and so now Congress should remove the tool that was weaponized against the American people by the Biden administration. That was in fact the face act. It was passed in the mid 1990s. It has been used overwhelmingly by those forces directed at pro-life people. only in a handful of instances that have been used in the context of other scenarios. And so we find it to be something that would be permanently changed if we were to pass the face act. And that's why I introduced legislation, why Mike leads this legislation. It's not enough for us to reverse damage. We need to prevent future abuse. And that's why the face act is so important.",
