    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46642.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "I wanna point out something very important and we're gonna get to some other pieces of legislation that you have introduced, reintroduced this week and this new session as well, but you recall that there was a time in the 2024 election cycle where there were some folks who very committed to the life movement had some, started to have some misgivings about then-candidate Donald Trump. What does his robust activity on the life movement in, you know, let's face it, it's been a very ambitious week already, a very active week already, but do you think those misgivings are disappearing now with what we're seeing from this president?",
