  {
    "episode_id": 46642,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46642.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, I certainly think it is hard for anyone to see someone who has been president of the United States who has done more for life than what President Trump has done. Obviously, the Supreme Court, and then what resulted with respect to reversing Roe. But I think being the first sitting president to go address the March for Life, what, four or five years ago, now seeing what's happening here with these pardons, And look, I think the president has positioned himself in what I would say is the right place. And I say that as someone who is passionately and ardently pro-life, believed life begins a conception, I believe that we should go protect life. But the president is right politically that if we want to go win and save lives, that's the point of being pro-life, then we need to go move minds and hearts. And I think you do that best by staying in the confines of what we've been arguing for half a century, right? Allowing people and their legislatures and states to determine and figure out how they want to manage a lot of this, but then pushing back on the abuses of the federal government. In other words, depoliticize that. Either something that's critically important to what President Trump has done, the secret sauce, is to try to actually depoliticize a lot of the stuff in the weaponization of what's gone on in Washington, to really restore the ability of people to make these decisions. And look, that flew in the face a little bit of some of our art into pro-life supporters and friends. who wanted a quick reaction to what happened in reversing Roe by coming in and saying, we need immediately a 10-week or 12-week or 15-week ban. And the president, I think, was correct. And by the way, I stood up and said that at the time, and I got some arrows from the pro-life flank who have been big supporters of mine. And so did the president. I think the president was correct. And, you know, I was happy to go move the Border Live Act today because we're talking about equal protection laws for those children that are born in, that are sitting in a hospital and the right of that child to get health care. I mean, the filibuster here, but I think that is the long and the short of the president.",
