    "turn_text": "So we just had that debate for an hour on the floor. I was running the floor on that for Republicans. So I can tell you precisely the arguments that Democrats were making, and that was that they wanted to make it all about abortion. I was focused, as were my colleagues, on my side of the aisle, focusing on the extent to which you have a American citizen, a fellow American, a fellow human being, in the form of a child that is born and that is being denied life-saving treatment for political purposes for my colleagues on the other side of the aisle, and you literally can't frame it any other way. And my college outside did not want to talk about that at all. They just wanted to bring it back to abortion, and abortion right. And the fact is we just had the vote on the House floor. We had, I think the final vote was 217 to 204 in one present. You only had one yes vote for Democrats, one present vote for Democrats, 204 no votes. All Republicans voted yes, except for two or not voting. So on my point being, there were nine non-voting for Democrats. So we passed it. We will send it over to the Senate now. That does not appear to vote well on the Senate side. I think they had their own vote over there. And I don't know how the vote actually unfolded, but I think it was maybe 52 to 47 or something like that. But which means you had a majority support, but that's not enough to overcome the 60 vote threshold in the Senate.",
