    "turn_text": "Well, the same act as an important bill. It was a bill that was placed in and embedded in our initial rules package. I hope that we will be bringing that up and calling it up for a vote reasonably soon. We obviously passed it out of the House last July with a hand, it was a bipartisan bill. We got a handful of folks who supported that. I think we got five, maybe who joined along with that bill to pass it out, but five Democrats. We are hopeful that we can move it soon, get it over to the Senate. Chuck Schumer wouldn't move it, obviously. This said it would be more implied to move it. I think if it got a vote on the floor, they'd have a tough time of not having at least seven Democrats joined it to vote for it. There are other matters we want to maybe add to it, or pass a different bill or companion legislation. Remember, the same act was designed very specifically last summer to require a documentary group of citizenship for voting, for registering to vote. There are things we'd like to do with respect to the census and the data we collect, there's legislation that we would like",
